Subject: [PATCH 09743/11362] [outer-loop] Disposition two claim-audit
 findings: strawman-baseline class

exp6544 and exp6546 both drew CLAIM_OVERSTATED on 2026-08-23. Both are
ACCEPTED. They share a shape distinct from the earlier exp6478/exp6497
rows, and naming it is the point of writing these up.

Those earlier two were circular: the verifier WAS the oracle, which the
existing lint catches once verdict_class is declared. These two declare
verifier_is_oracle: false correctly and are genuinely oracle-distinct.
What is wrong is the baseline. In exp6544 the stop rule guarantees the
analytical arm wins, and no_headroom_pair_count is 0 across 54 pairs --
a comparison where no pair lacks headroom had no serious baseline. In
exp6546 routed Z3 calls carry no token charge, so routing work to Z3
lowers the measured cost by definition, and Z3 cannot be less correct
than the model under the stated evaluation, so non-inferiority is
guaranteed rather than observed.

Both measurements stand; neither is headline-eligible, and neither shows
the added value it claims. The missing controls are named in the ledger:
a deepest-first deterministic baseline for exp6544, an always-Z3 arm for
exp6546. No lint detects a strawman baseline, and building one is not
obviously cheap -- "was this baseline a real threat" is a judgement the
claim audit already makes better than a pattern match would.

Artifacts left unedited per never-prune.

Recovered the exp6546 reasoning from commit 1d35738746: the conductor
overwrites the claim-audit report at each milestone-close, so a ledger
row can outlive the report that explains it. Recorded in the row itself.

